{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526739-broken-leg","id":1526739,"title":"Broken Leg","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-13T06:15:45-08:00","id":1526739,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Broken Leg","content":"During a chronicle something that could possibly happen is that a PC gets hurt and in the worst case is mutilated, however in MTA I've seen someone mention that, even with great difficulty, a human body can be replicated, so I believe that generating a new leg or arm is relatively easier, that said, it would be possible to recover an amputated limb, but the point I want to get is wouldn't it also be possible to improve you body? I imagine that the Sons of Ether and the Virtual Adepts would use robotic limbs and other traditions would think about doing something similar even if in a different way, now my thought is how would this translate mechanically? To what extent would this be acceptable? In addition to the interaction with the spheres, I imagine it would have to be at a high level. What are your ideas?<br /> <br /> In a parallel aspect, how would you deal with a kind of supernatural contamination, like something coming from the Nephandi, influences from the Umbra like the Weaver, or even the Jhor caused by Entropy (Which I admit to being a little confused by it.)\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T06:52:58-08:00","id":1526745,"title":"","content":"Physical improvements is what the Enhancements Background is all about. Don't buy the line about it being exclusive to the Technocracy; I'd be okay, for example, with a mage who tattoos mystical runes on herself representing them as an Enhancement. This is, after all, what the original Blessing Background was in MRev before Brucato missed the point and completely rewrote it.<br /> <br /> That sort of thing is definitely in the purview of Life; and the only reason why it isn't ubiquitous is because of Permanent Paradox, Genetic Flaws, or the like: it seems that when you try to rush nature, it tends to push back.<br /> <br /> I do think that more subtle changes could be integrated into the body without the usual downsides of an Enhancement, such as permanently acquiring a dot in Strength or Stamina. But doing so requires time, which I would represent in game as earning XPs and spending them to purchase the dot.<br /> <br /> And it needn't be restricted to physical changes: \u201cI know Kung Fu\u201d from <i>The Matrix</i> could be implemented as an Enhancement (or Requisition) operating through Mind, with the ability to instantly install a skill in the mage's head, but at the cost of Permadox/Flaws. Do it more gradually, and you can avoid the downsides; it simply becomes a flavorful way of spending XPs on more Ability dots.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-30-2023, 07:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T07:08:46-08:00","id":1526748,"title":"","content":"I could have sworn that was a rule, that using magic to get permanent buffs that you could have bought with XP gains Permadox until you do buy it with XP. I might be thinking of Revised or Mage: the Awakening, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T07:30:53-08:00","id":1526751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526739-broken-leg?p=1526745#post1526745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Physical improvements is what the Enhancements Background is all about. Don't buy the line about it being exclusive to the Technocracy; I'd be okay, for example, with a mage who tattoos mystical runes on herself representing them as an Enhancement. This is, after all, what the original Blessing Background was in MRev before Brucato missed the point and completely rewrote it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that this wouldn't be something exclusively technocratic, but I think it's difficult for traditions other than the Sons of Ether, Virtual Adepts and Hermetics to think about doing something like that, the cult and the Euthanatos I think it is difficult unleast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526739-broken-leg?p=1526745#post1526745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sort of thing is definitely in the preview of Life; and the only reason why it isn't ubiquitous is because of Permanent Paradox, Genetic Flaws, or the like: it seems that when you try to rush nature, it tends to push back.<br /> <br /> I do think that more subtle changes could be integrated into the body without the usual downsides of an Enhancement, such as permanently acquiring a dot in Strength or Stamina. But doing so requires time, which I would represent in game as earning XPs and spending them to purchase the dot.<br /> <br /> And it needn't be restricted to physical changes: \u201cI know Kung Fu\u201d from <i>The Matrix</i> could be implemented as an Enhancement (or Requisition) operating through Mind, with the ability to instantly install a skill in the mage's head, but at the cost of Permadox/Flaws. Do it more gradually, and you can avoid the downsides; it simply becomes a flavorful way of spending XPs on more Ability dots.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is more about you narratively justifying a change that would not normally occur with your character, rather than making changes to the body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T08:20:06-08:00","id":1526756,"title":"","content":"Kind of. The difference is that the means that you use to make the change don't have to be mundane. \u201cI'm going to put this sleep-teacher device on my head every night until I've learned some more Martial Arts\u201d is perfectly valid for a mage with the right Focus to do, even though sleep-teacher devices aren't something that actually works in mundane reality.<br /> <br /> Or, in terms of physical changes, you might undergo a regimen of performance-boosting super-drugs that ever so gradually increase your Strength and Stamina. No need to pump iron; just give the drugs time to do their work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-13-2023, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T09:31:53-08:00","id":1526764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526739-broken-leg?p=1526748#post1526748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could have sworn that was a rule, that using magic to get permanent buffs that you could have bought with XP gains Permadox until you do buy it with XP. I might be thinking of Revised or Mage: the Awakening, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct. It's on page 22 of <b>How Do You DO That?</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-20T16:31:11-08:00","id":1527135,"title":"","content":"&quot;It's not as bad as it looked&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T15:15:59-08:00","id":1527789,"title":"","content":"I think there's also a route to a Sanctum dojo/retreat/spa/whatever where you magick yourself stronger, faster, smarter, sexier with any outright Vulgar means, but spend the XP before you come out, no Paradox side effects. That would open up more options for other Traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}